  "worked_solution": "The graph of $y=f(x-1)$ is a horizontal translation of the graph of $y=f(x)$ by $1$ unit to the *right*. So, every point on the graph of $y=f(x-1)$ is one unit *to the right* of the corresponding point on the graph of $y=f(x).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14214993/assets/96e78d86fc113988887c0c35daf2ebf119f2f47be8d82822d439b2f47433c31d.png)",
